  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (config_004, 0.5203 acc) outperforms pca_n2000 (config_001, 0.4849 acc) as an RNA encoder, and image-only (config_010, 0.2079 acc) is very weak, suggesting RNA modality drives performance. Uncertainty: it is unknown whether multiprofile aggregation adds value on top of the best singleprofile encoder. This experiment (config_005: rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean one-variable extension of the current best (config_004), isolating the effect of multiprofile + avgpool aggregation while holding the encoder constant. It is the best use of this slot because the multiprofile/aggregation question is structurally central—it determines whether 20+ downstream multiprofile and multimodal configurations are worth pursuing, and answering it early with a simple aggregation (avgpool) before trying transformer keeps the comparison interpretable and conserves budget for later exploitation."
}

